  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-06T10:38:42.906Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As the title implies, would it be possible to have a scene descriptor option to disable avatar changing as well just like there's an option to disable portal drops? One problem people face when playing the game maps I make is how people just love to constantly switch avatars trying to show off their collection etc. Considering that the world I make is based on reaction and reflex as well, it's quite troublesome and bothersome when the frame drops and the music goes out of sync compared to what's happening on the play stage. I use music heavily too especially as a form of cue for players on what to do next. It's even worse when the other player loads in a heavily non-optimized avatar and because of this-- it does force some of the player to resort to having to make a private instance.",
